# tail(1)

## NAME

tail - output the last part of files

## SYNOPSIS

    tail [-n [+]lines] [file...]

## DESCRIPTION

Writes the last 10 lines of each file (or standard input). With `+N`, writes from line N to the end. `-f` is not supported.

## OPTIONS

- `-n lines`: number of lines (also `-lines`)

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

